#entry("builder:WP-03", "interface", status: "final")[*Kleene semantics for WP-04 (Lean mirror):* missing or `'unknown'` facts are unknown; strong Kleene `and`/`or`/`not`, empty `and` true, empty `or` false; `cmp`/`in` unknown if any operand unknown; booleans compare as 1/0 (so a Tri fact is written `{ cmp: '=', left: { fact }, right: 1 }`); strings allow only `=`/`!=`, a number never equals a string, other mixes are malformed; a named function with no implementation is unknown. Status: `blocked` if a block is true or a needed check is recorded `fail`; else `needs-check` if a block is unknown or a `check` effect (condition true or unknown) has no record; else `feasible`. A recorded `pass` or `conditional` (latest `at` wins) satisfies a check. `consent`, `oblige`, `warn` apply when true or unknown (worst case). Dates are inclusive both ends. M0-4 mutant: `UK.DNO.HP.LOOPED` on GH1 (looped unknown) gives `needs-check`, so a GH1 heat pump package marked feasible must fail `feas.recompute`.]
